{"name":"Arterial","hex":"#711518","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arterial","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to an artery.","Major, important."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high-capacity urban road."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arterial"}],"entries":[{"title":"Artery","blocks":[{"text":"An artery is a blood vessel in humans and most other animals that takes oxygenated blood away from the heart in the systemic circulation to one or more parts of the body. Exceptions that carry deoxygenated blood are the pulmonary arteries in the pulmonary circulation that carry blood to the lungs for oxygenation, and the umbilical arteries in the fetal circulation that carry deoxygenated blood to the placenta. It consists of a multi-layered artery wall wrapped into a tube-shaped channel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Artery.svg/330px-Artery.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artery","wikidata":"Q9655"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png/500px-Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png/1280px-Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png/500px-Blausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Microscopic anatomy of an artery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlausen_0055_ArteryWallStructure.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Artery.png/500px-Artery.png?utm_source=en.wik